{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/794675-how-are-the-unseelie-just-as-noble-and-honorable-as-their-seelie-counterparts","id":794675,"title":"HOW are the Unseelie \"just as noble and honorable as their Seelie counterparts?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-29T01:12:45-08:00","id":794675,"title":"HOW are the Unseelie \"just as noble and honorable as their Seelie counterparts?\"","content":"Dear White Wolf<br /> Refreshing my knowledge on Changeling The Dreaming by looking through the old rulebooks.<br /> One aspect has been bugging me a LOT.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Legacies&quot; section describes on &quot;The Unseelie can be just as noble and honorable as their Seelie counterparts&quot;<br /> And then it goes STRAIGHT into a litany of hateful, cynical and selfish personalities that gains willpower from hurting people, destroying hope, disrupting society and inconsiderate self-gratification at best.<br /> <br /> Their mission in life is explicitly stated to be: Make the world a colder, sadder, more cynical and mean spirited place by destroying hope and creating nightmares. And treating helpless mortals as no more than cattle and toys the same way Sabbat Vampires do.<br /> <br /> And it gets WORSE. Expansions state that Unseelie Fae consider the below to be acceptable allies and even AGREEABLE FRIENDS.<br /> <br /> Sabbat (Sociopathic Sadistic Rapists)<br /> Nepandi (Sociopathic Megalomanic Rapists)<br /> Specters (Sociopathy Incarnate)<br /> and Worst of All<br /> Black-Fucking-Spiral Dancers (CANNIBALISTIC INCESTUOUS Sociopathic Rapists)<br /> <br /> And that's not taking into account the basic Unseelie's Code of &quot;Morality&quot; (if it can even be called that)<br /> <br /> &quot;Change Is Good&quot; (&quot;Promises are made to be broken&quot;)<br /> &quot;Glamour is Free&quot; (&quot;I can bully mortals and treat them as Glamor Happy Meals how ever I see fit!&quot;)<br /> &quot;Honor is A Lie&quot; (DIRECT Contradiction to the opening statement)<br /> &quot;Passion Before Duty&quot; (&quot;Me Me Me! Screw everyone else!&quot;)<br /> <br /> How in ANY sane way can one consider Unseelie, who are PROUD of being Cynical, sadistic, self-centered, oath-breaking, hope-destroying, sociopathic, nihilistic, raping, murdering bullies-of-the-weak-and-helpless who REGULARLY (and literally) share beds with other sadistic rapists to be &quot;Noble and Honorable&quot; in ANY way shape and form?<br /> <br /> That is as &quot;heroic&quot; in the same way that the hateful savages and animals of &quot;joe-pee-pee-maltin's play-of-chairs&quot; can be considered &quot;human beings.&quot; (NOT sorry: Have ZERO respect WHATSOEVER for elitist crap that encourages its readers/viewers to ignore/mock/hold-in-contempt Asian Heroes/Hopes-and-Dreams)<br /> <br /> Ah contradictions, contradictions.<br /> <br /> Looking Forward To Playing My TRULY Noble and Honorable Troll Defender for &quot;Changeling 20&quot;<br /> <br /> TASTE MY HAMMER! VILLAIN! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> NO INNOCENT BLOOD WILL BE SPILT AS LONG AS I STAND!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 12-29-2015, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T03:23:45-08:00","id":794730,"title":"","content":"Well, some of that's the old White Wolf writing. The temptation has always been to see the Unseelie as the bad guys . . . But Seelie and Unseelie just don't translate well into &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot;. In traditional mythology, the Unseelie Court stood for the outsiders and rebels, the ugly, chaos and change, night, as well as the seasons of fall and winter. <br /> <br /> Sure, the Unseelie tend to see humans as disposable . . . but at least they're honest about it. A Seelie changeling can be just as much a monster as an Unseelie, they just put more effort into looking beautiful and elegant while doing so. <br /> <br /> And the better White Wolf authors took that into account. The core group of heroes in the <i>Immortal Eyes</i> novels, for example, was split roughly fifty-fifty between the two Courts. Does anyone doubt that Rasputin (the rabbit pooka) or Valmont (the eshu) were good guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T04:30:10-08:00","id":794756,"title":"","content":"Yeah, bad writing that will hopefully be fixed by C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T15:10:58-08:00","id":795122,"title":"","content":"The Summer Court and the Winter Court of Jim Butcher's Dresden Files series are a good example of how you can view the Seelie and the Unseelie Courts. Just because you're viewed as technically &quot;good&quot; doesn't mean you aren't capable of some truly heinous acts, and just because you're &quot;evil&quot; doesn't mean you can't do things that fit a purpose that isn't personally beneficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T17:28:50-08:00","id":795223,"title":"","content":"The Unseelie are honorable in that they are <i>honest</i>. The world is a cold, cruel, dangerous place. The Seelie will pretend to a false veneer of civilization, all the while looking for an excuse to blame you when they decide to torture, maim, and murder you. The Unseelie tell you outright what they're about, and they make no bones about it. They're better allies, because when they say they're on your side, they actually mean it. They won't pretend to noble intentions they do not have; they'll tell you outright what your mutual interest with them is, and at what point they'll turn on you. It won't even be betrayal; they let you know long in advance.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean there aren't dishonorable Unseelie Changelings who'll lie, cheat, steal, and deceive, but they certainly <b>can</b> be just as honorable as the most honestly honorable of the Seelie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T18:21:13-08:00","id":795273,"title":"","content":"Though the &quot;Noble&quot; part of the equation still is not solved.<br /> &quot;Noble&quot; requires one to be able to feel compassion for those less fortunate than you,<br /> And requires one to be capable of love, kindness, selflessness and sacrifice.<br /> Virtues that the *proudly-selfish* Unseelie openly lack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T19:01:23-08:00","id":795295,"title":"","content":"That's one definition of noble, sure. The Seelie definition. <br /> <br /> Nobility is just an adherence to moral principles. The difference comes in just what the Unseelie find moral, versus what the Seelie do. One moral might be &quot;forgiveness is divine, forgetfulness is idiotic&quot;. Another might be &quot;suffer not the weak to hold power&quot;. Morals and ethics cover a wide variety of ground. Don't get too tangled up in what is, essentially, a one-sided definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T08:35:06-08:00","id":796853,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">What can I say, my Unseelie Legacy is Sophist: <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/noble\" target=\"_blank\">Noble</a></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T14:05:57-08:00","id":797009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/794675-how-are-the-unseelie-just-as-noble-and-honorable-as-their-seelie-counterparts?p=795295#post795295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one definition of noble, sure. The Seelie definition.<br /> <br /> Nobility is just an adherence to moral principles. The difference comes in just what the Unseelie find moral, versus what the Seelie do. One moral might be &quot;forgiveness is divine, forgetfulness is idiotic&quot;. Another might be &quot;suffer not the weak to hold power&quot;. Morals and ethics cover a wide variety of ground. Don't get too tangled up in what is, essentially, a one-sided definition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where does the Seelie code show anything resembling compassion? The seelie very much can be a pretty world with no place for the broken. The Seelie demand perfection. The Unseelie accept you for your flaws or at least that's how I view it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T04:30:45-08:00","id":797744,"title":"","content":"But are there any cases/examples of these S.O.Bs being capable of ACTUAL heroism, nobility and kindness rather than the hateful and distorted &quot;I am the greatest devil in a world of devils&quot; crap that HBO's glorified snuff film for TV series joe-pee-pee-maltin's &quot;play-of-chairs&quot; expects the world to swallow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-01-2016, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T10:51:46-08:00","id":797868,"title":"","content":"A peacock who defines their glory by the praise of others will easily be driven to all manner of acts of heroism. A pandora explorer or Crusading journalist type. Those are just 3 off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Though I do agree the Unseelie legacies could use a dash more neutrality, a Beast who could defend &quot;what's mine&quot; through the same brutality but without being defined by hurting everything around him would work better. WIth a little work I could see it being the &quot;Hot blooded Shonen protagonist Legacy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-01-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T11:02:29-08:00","id":800650,"title":"","content":"&quot;Nobility&quot; doesn't inherently mean &quot;charitable&quot; or &quot;kind.&quot; It is in theory supposed to, but it can also mean &quot;regal&quot; or &quot;grand.&quot; At the same time, the Unseelie who chooses to forsake genteelity could still be honorable and even kind, perhaps simply doing so grubbily or &quot;getting his hands dirty&quot; in a way the 'noble' Seelie would never do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T02:05:47-08:00","id":801225,"title":"","content":"This is why I can't wait for the Legacies to be rewritten. I always just reverted to using Natures and Demeanors, since the Legacies are so broken. One way around it is to houserule that every Legacy can be either Seelie or Unseelie, and reinterpret them as appropriate. But that requires more work than just using Natures and Demeanors, which can emulate most of the Legacies anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:20:23-08:00","id":801324,"title":"","content":"My personal favorite Sidhe concept is rather unassuming (for a Sidhe) as a Seelie noble youth, but his Unseelie mein is terrifying but very noble. As The Lord of Winter, he has Beast as his Legacy, but is the very controlled, genteel monster that hides behind a cold aloofness. He believes that it is foolish of the Seelie to try to stave off winter, as it is inevitable, and stupid of the majority of Unseelie to fritter away time like the proverbial grasshopper, hoping to enjoy things before Winter comes and freezes them.<br /> <br /> No, he believes that Winter is not a bad thing, because after Winter comes Spring. And so he exhorts stockpiling glamour while (more in the public eye, because of what the terrified masses focus on) he seeks to deliberately bring Winter crashing down. The harsher the Winter, the sooner the Spring. And so he'll destroy that which is holding it up and making the Autumn stretch so untenably long.<br /> <br /> He's been called an ally of the Autumn People; but the Lord of Winter should terrify them as much as any other, for only by ending their season can his begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T16:49:22-08:00","id":801668,"title":"","content":"Because the beltaine massacre made Seelie Sidhe honor a bad joke?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T19:25:46-08:00","id":801733,"title":"","content":"Unseelie were pretty much evil. I can't claim otherwise. In setting, the idea was that they were some shades of grey sort of character, but it really just doesn't stand up.<br /> <br /> That said, there are a few non-evil Legacies, particularly Fatalist, Fool, Grotesque, Pandora, Riddler, Savage and Wretch, although I'd be hard pressed to call any of them noble. Beast, Knave, and Outlaw seem especially prone to wickedness, while Peacock, Rake, Ringleader, and Rogue don't seem inherently evil but definitely prone to asshole qualities.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie code is fairly strongly neutral; the above interpretations are quite uncharitable. It would be easy to twist the Seelie code too:<br /> <br /> <i>Death Before Dishoner:</i> Note it doesn't say your death. Under such interpretation, it's perfectly acceptable to have someone killed if it means preserving your honor.<br /> <br /> <i>Love Conquers All</i>: Throw away literally everything because someone gave you a boner. Sure, marry the evil queen. Surely love will make her stop being a despicable tyrant. Sure, fulfill that suicide pact with the boy you meet a week ago; the lives you destroyed weren't people who really loved you or anything.<br /> <br /> <i>Beauty is Life:</i> But beauty is not synonymous with goodness.<br /> <br /> <i>Never forget a debt:</i> Or forgive a cruelty. Make sure everything is an eternal blood feud. Leave the world blind and toothless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T22:42:56-08:00","id":801813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/794675-how-are-the-unseelie-just-as-noble-and-honorable-as-their-seelie-counterparts?p=801225#post801225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I can't wait for the Legacies to be rewritten. I always just reverted to using Natures and Demeanors, since the Legacies are so broken. One way around it is to houserule that every Legacy can be either Seelie or Unseelie, and reinterpret them as appropriate. But that requires more work than just using Natures and Demeanors, which can emulate most of the Legacies anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I&quot;ve been thinking about using Nature for WP and modified Legacy for Glamor<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T17:32:53-08:00","id":802481,"title":"","content":"There's an old saying (which the game even quoted at one point) about the fae being &quot;too good for Hell, but not good enough for Heaven&quot;. Sure, the Seelie Court upholds honor . . . but its not &quot;honor&quot; in the sense that the average human would recognize it. The fae were always the ultimate rules-lawyers, finding every loophole, twisting words and promises to their own advantage.<br /> <br /> Consider an oath to protect Person X's life &quot;to the last breath&quot;. By the rules of Seelie honor, a Seelie fae could stand aside while Person X is tortured - as long their life isn't in danger, they've kept their oath. The Seelie could turn Person X into a rabbit, and keep them in a cage for their rest of their life - again, permitted under their oath. The Seelie could even kill Person X themselves, as long as they do it before Person X draws another breath (because then Person X has already drawn their &quot;last breath&quot;). And of course suffocation or drowning. . .<br /> <br /> Traditionally, the Seelie Court stood for beauty, the establishment, the seasons of spring and summer, day, and the forces of order and tradition. But they never stood for good. Individual Seelie, sure, but not the Court as a whole. To truly be good, they'd have to care about the truth. And the truth is often ugly. And ugly things are Unseelie by definition<br /> <br /> At their worst, the Seelie are all about &quot;rule of the prettiest&quot;. They're the cool kids who shunned you because you didn't have the latest fashions, because your parents couldn't afford to buy you a car . . . the ones who looked down on you, even as they asked for your help.<br /> <br /> The Seelie are the kind of people who ignore that Count Fancypants is beating his wife, rather than deal with the truth. Or - horror of horrors - not be invited to the Count's next party. Because its an ugly situation, and - if they admit its happening - they have to kick him out of court. Because beating your wife is ugly . . . and thus he'd be Unseelie in their eyes. Better instead to teach her how to hide her injuries behind illusions, and just pretend it isn't happening. That way, the beauty of their court/freehold/etc isn't disrupted, and no one's feelings have to be hurt.<br /> <br /> (That's not to say the local Unseelie fae would care - they might or they might not. But at least they won't lie to your face, and deny that its happening.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/794675-how-are-the-unseelie-just-as-noble-and-honorable-as-their-seelie-counterparts?p=797009#post797009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where does the Seelie code show anything resembling compassion? The seelie very much can be a pretty world with no place for the broken. The Seelie demand perfection. The Unseelie accept you for your flaws or at least that's how I view it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some stories even say that's how the Unseelie got started. The Seelie Court started evicting anyone who was ugly or unpopular, and at some point, there got to be enough exiles that they started their own competing court. Hence the name &quot;Unseelie&quot; - literally, &quot;Not Seelie&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: On an interesting side note, the Seelie might be responsible for global warming. The nature of the ruler influences the local weather, and the two courts are supposed to switch off every six months. But ever since the sidhe returned, the Seelie have refused to relinquish control the Unseelie. So its been over forty years of endless summer (or at least fae magic pushing the weather in that direction)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-06-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T17:46:02-08:00","id":802494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/794675-how-are-the-unseelie-just-as-noble-and-honorable-as-their-seelie-counterparts?p=801813#post801813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I&amp;quot;ve been thinking about using Nature for WP and modified Legacy for Glamor</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea. Do you have a particular system for this? Do the characters still have two Legacies? Do they have Demeanor as well as Nature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T23:31:41-08:00","id":802815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/794675-how-are-the-unseelie-just-as-noble-and-honorable-as-their-seelie-counterparts?p=802494#post802494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good idea. Do you have a particular system for this? Do the characters still have two Legacies? Do they have Demeanor as well as Nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demeanor I can take or leave. Character would have two legacies. Based on court/camp/etc. You get WP when you do Nature stuff. you Get Glamour when you'd get WP normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:56:37-08:00","id":804029,"title":"","content":"The problem with Unseelie=bad is that people forget that the Seelie aren't good, but do remember that the Unseelie and Seelie are rough opposites.<br /> <br /> You should ideally be able to phrase a concept in the terms of each court. They might not be identical, but they will be equivalent. Think of a social worker or journalist in both Seelie and Unseelie terms. Try for a detective or a businessman. The 'good guy' concept doesn't always fall on Seelie side.<br /> <br /> Instead of black and white, think of the Seelie as light and dark. Sometimes it's better to be in the sun, and sometimes you'd prefer the shade.<br /> <br /> Not that 'sociopathic X' is a bad description of an Unseelie's friends, it does describe a lot of Seelie as well though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:24:34-08:00","id":806261,"title":"","content":"A Seelie social worker is going to work hard to place people in exactly the right job for them. He will seek to give them positions which they look good in, and which reflect well on her and the organization. He will encourage proper appearance and manners, and that only decorous habits be practiced (though the habits themselves need only be made proper for presentation). He will look down on his more slovenly clients, insisting they elevate themselves to his standards or he will...dispose of them.<br /> <br /> An Unseelie social worker will make sure that you have every loophole exploited to your advantage, and will place people where they think they'll have the best time. Decorum be darned, if you're happier getting your hands dirty, they'll place you there. They won't stand on ceremony nor expect you to, and will not look down on people for their appearance, but won't necessarily encourage a better one unless it helps them directly. More likely to let people lay on a hammock of social welfare, they also aren't as likely to shoehorn people into an unsuitable mold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:52:33-07:00","id":849910,"title":"","content":"Looked like a good place to ask a question I had a bit ago, if a Unseelie feels personal affection for a person, changeling or mortal, is it safe to say their affection would be as passionate as their other emotions, but that their largess might be almost dangerous even if its honestly meant.<br /> <br /> Also another point? <br /> <br /> House Leahaun Trys to treat their Rhapsody victims with nothing short of love, ideally, even to repay the debt by watching over their children and widows, not all do but enough do its considered polite.<br /> <br /> It doesnt make the practice RIGHT but it shows their not absolute and utter monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T12:46:18-07:00","id":850748,"title":"","content":"Unseelie are no more or less dangerous in their affection than Seelie, honestly. The difference between the two is one largely of <i>what</i> formality they follow. The Unseelie put less stock in appearances, but they are sticklers for forms. They just allow and accept grotesqueries as part of them. The Seelie are exquisite, no matter what they're doing. The Unseelie are primal, no matter what they're doing. But both are formal. Both are passionate. Both are dangerous...but the latter are more obviously so than the former.<br /> <br /> Being a beloved of an Unseelie can actually be safer, in some circumstances, than being the beloved of a Seelie. The Unseelie will protect their beloved even from their own court, possibly by defying its intrigues. If only because its intrigues are less Byzantine due to the formalities more readily accepting violent resolution to disputes. The Seelie will protect their beloved, but if the Court and its rules tie a noose around his neck, she'll weep an exquisite tear of sorrow as she watches him be sacrificed on the altar of formality rather than break those rules in an ugly display.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T13:36:42-07:00","id":850781,"title":"","content":"To provide some of the Examples requested. <br /> The characters in a campaign have sworn an oath that later in game causes a problem, adhering to the oath would lead to a tragedy that none of he characters wish to see, however the seelie changelings cannot act as they would like as doing so would mean dishonour. This is pretty bad. The Unseelie however may act as they wish since 'honour is a lie' and while (depending on the oath and the power behind it) they may suffer effects for Oathbreaking they can intercede in alignment with their desires. <br /> <br /> There is a chimerae or nightmare or so etching terrorising the local community. The local Freeholds are mostly dominated by the Seelie Sidhe lords and the dreamers that provide Glamour or Dross to the Sidhe are not effected by the threat, neither are the Seelie Sidhe threatened. However the Commoners see this as more than a nuisance and decide to try and deal with it, this requires Glamour, but the Seelie are unwilling to use up the stores of magic they are accumulating and the commoners struggle to wield their magics against the dangers pressing at them. A local Unseelie noble of House Balor however opens her freehold to the most determined and fierce of the would be monster hunters and dragon slayers, gifts them dross and encourages the ravaging of the dreamers she knows of, winter is a little closer perhaps, but the changelings have the magical power to face down the threat. <br /> <br /> Your character owes a Seelie changeling a favour and they come calling to collect. Through no fault of your own you cannot complete the favour and the friend you once had turns bitter and spurns you, fault doesn't matter as the favour was not returned. Conversely an Unseelie fae may need a favour of you but may be reasoned with if you cannot come through on the deal due to circumstances not of your control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}